Title: Game Controls
Author: André Fernandes
Color: 3D2518

# Chapter: Moving Around

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/W.png,Assets/Resources/Images/A.png,Assets/Resources/Images/S.png,Assets/Resources/Images/D.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Left Analogue.png

- Move around using the [WASD] keys on your keyboard or the left analogue stick on your gamepad!

# Chapter: Looking Around

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Mouse.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Right Analogue.png

- To look around, move your mouse or use the right analogue stick on your gamepad!

# Chapter: Dodge Roll / Backstep

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Shift.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Button East (PS4).png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Button East (Xbox).png

- Tap the button while moving to perform a dodge roll. This helps you avoid damage but consumes stamina.
<> [br]
<> [br]
<> Tap the button while standing still to perform a backstep.

# Chapter: Sprinting

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Shift.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Button East (PS4).png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Button East (Xbox).png

- Hold the button to sprint! On a gamepad, you can also press the left analogue stick while moving to start sprinting.
<> [br]
<> Sprinting consumes stamina while active.

# Chapter: Light Attack

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Left Mouse.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/R1 (PS4).png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/R1 (Xbox).png

- Tap the button to perform a light attack.
<> [br]
<> The stamina cost depends on the weapon equipped.

# Chapter: Heavy Attack

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/G.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/R2 (PS4).png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/R2 (Xbox).png

- Tap the button to perform a heavy attack.
<> [br]
<> Heavy attacks deal more damage than light ones but consume more stamina.

# Chapter: Jumping

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Spacebar.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Button South (PS4).png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Button South (Xbox).png

- Jumping allows you to reach higher places.
<> [br]
<> Be cautious—jumping from great heights can cause fall damage!

# Chapter: Jump Attack

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Spacebar.png,Assets/Resources/Images/Add.png,Assets/Resources/Images/Left Mouse.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Button South (PS4).png,Assets/Resources/Images/Add.png,Assets/Resources/Images/R1 (PS4).png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Button South (Xbox).png,Assets/Resources/Images/Add.png,Assets/Resources/Images/R1 (Xbox).png

- Press the attack button while in mid-air to perform a jumping attack! This also works when falling from a height.

# Chapter: Sprint Attack

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Shift.png,Assets/Resources/Images/Add.png,Assets/Resources/Images/Left Mouse.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Button East (PS4).png,Assets/Resources/Images/Add.png,Assets/Resources/Images/R1 (PS4).png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Button East (Xbox).png,Assets/Resources/Images/Add.png,Assets/Resources/Images/R1 (Xbox).png

- Press the attack button while sprinting to perform a sprint attack!

# Chapter: Lock On

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Middle Mouse.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Right Analogue Click.png

- Tap to lock the camera onto an enemy (also known as z-targeting). This helps you focus on a single opponent during combat.

# Chapter: Lock On To Other Targets

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Mouse.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Right Analogue Move.png

- When facing multiple enemies, you can switch targets by gently moving your mouse left or right,
<>or by nudging the right analogue stick in the desired direction.

# Chapter: Quick Items

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Quick Items.png

- Equip certain items via the main menu for quick access during gameplay.
<>[br]
<>[br]
<>Upward Slot: Used to switch spells  
<>[br]
<>Downward Slot: Used to switch consumables (e.g., potions)  
<>[br]
<>Right: Used to switch right-hand weapons  
<>[br]
<>Left: Used to switch left-hand weapons  
<>[br]

# Chapter: Switch Spells

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Quick Items - Spell.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/2.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Directional Pad - Up (PS4).png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Directional Pad - Up (Xbox).png

- Press [2] or the up arrow on your keyboard, or the up button on your gamepad’s directional pad, to switch spells.
<>[br]

# Chapter: Use Spell

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Q.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/L2 (PS4).png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/L2 (Xbox).png

- Press [Q] or [L2] to cast a spell.
<>[br]
<>[br]
<>Spells are powerful abilities that scale with the Intelligence stat, which can be upgraded at a bonfire.
<>[br]
<>[br]
<>Casting spells usually consumes mana.

# Chapter: Switch Consumable

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Quick Items - Consumables.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/4.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Directional Pad - Down (PS4).png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Directional Pad - Down (Xbox).png

- Press [4] or the down arrow on your keyboard, or the down button on your gamepad’s directional pad, to cycle through consumables.
<>[br]
<> Equip items such as potions, firebombs, and weapon buffs (e.g., elemental resins).

# Chapter: Use Consumable

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/R.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Button North (PS4).png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Button North (Xbox).png

- Press [R] or the corresponding gamepad button to use the selected consumable.

# Chapter: Switch Right Weapon

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Quick Items - Right Weapon.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/3.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Directional Pad - Right (PS4).png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Directional Pad - Right (Xbox).png

- Press [3] or the right arrow on your keyboard, or the right button on your gamepad’s directional pad, to switch right-hand weapons.
<>[br]
<> You can equip up to three right-hand weapons!

# Chapter: Switch Left Weapon

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Quick Items - Left Weapon.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/1.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Directional Pad - Left (PS4).png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Directional Pad - Left (Xbox).png

- Press [1] or the left arrow on your keyboard, or the left button on your gamepad’s directional pad, to switch left-hand weapons.
<>[br]
<> You can equip up to three left-hand weapons!

# Chapter: Toggle Combat Stance

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Tab.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Share (PS4).png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Share (Xbox).png

- Press [TAB] or the [Share] button to toggle your combat stance.
<>[br]
<>This switches between one-handed mode (allowing left-hand equipment) and two-handed mode for increased right-hand weapon damage and different movesets.

# Chapter: Blocking

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Right Mouse.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/L1 (PS4).png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/L1 (Xbox).png

- Hold the right mouse button or [L1] to block.
<>[br]
<>You can block using your fists, a weapon, or ideally a shield equipped in the left hand.
<>[br]
<>[br]
<>[br]Some gear blocks 100% of damage, while others only reduce a portion based on their stats.
<>[br]
<>[br]
<>Blocking consumes stamina. If your stamina runs out, the block will fail.

# Chapter: Parrying

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Right Mouse.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/L1 (PS4).png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/L1 (Xbox).png

- Tap the right mouse button or [L1] just as an enemy attacks to parry.
<>[br]
<>Timing is key—successful parries prevent damage and increase the enemy’s posture bar (in yellow).
<>[br]
<>[br]When the bar fills, the enemy is staggered and vulnerable to a critical attack!

# Chapter: Block Attack

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Right Mouse.png,Assets/Resources/Images/Add.png,Assets/Resources/Images/Left Mouse.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/L1 (PS4).png,Assets/Resources/Images/Add.png,Assets/Resources/Images/R1 (PS4).png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/L1 (Xbox).png,Assets/Resources/Images/Add.png,Assets/Resources/Images/R1 (Xbox).png

- While blocking, press the attack button to strike without lowering your guard.
<>[br]
<>This is a balanced approach to stay defensive while keeping pressure on enemies!

# Chapter: Equipping Bow and Arrow

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Equipping Bow.png

- Bows and other ranged weapons can be equipped in the left-hand slot. Make sure to also equip suitable ammunition like arrows.

# Chapter: Aiming and Shooting Bows

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Aiming Bow.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Right Mouse.png,Assets/Resources/Images/Add.png,Assets/Resources/Images/Left Mouse.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/L1 (PS4).png,Assets/Resources/Images/Add.png,Assets/Resources/Images/R1 (PS4).png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/L1 (Xbox).png,Assets/Resources/Images/Add.png,Assets/Resources/Images/R1 (Xbox).png

- Hold the right mouse button or [L1] to aim your bow.
<>[br]
<>Then tap the attack button to shoot.

# Chapter: Control Camera Distance

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Middle Mouse.png

- Scroll the middle mouse button to adjust the camera distance (keyboard only).

# Chapter: Open Main Menu

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Esc.png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Options (PS4).png
# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Options (Xbox).png

- Press the buttons above to open the main menu.

# Chapter: Equipment Menu

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Equipment Menu.png

- By default, opening the main menu shows the Equipment Menu.
<>[br]
<>The left side displays currently equipped items.
<>[br]
<>The right side shows your character’s stats and attributes.

# Chapter: Quests Menu

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Quests Menu.png

- View your active quests in the Quests Menu.
<>[br]
<>You can track multiple quests at once—they’ll update automatically as you progress!

# Chapter: Settings Menu

# Images: Assets/Resources/Images/Settings Menu.png

- Adjust game settings, save your progress, or return to the title screen from the Settings Menu.
